  "translate_en|mods/Map Mod Manager/42.20/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/UI.json|UI_helpPanelText": "Map Mod Manager shows where your map mods sit on the world grid, so you can spot cell conflicts before you load a game.\n\nSUBSCRIBED MAP MODS\nYour installed map mods, split into Enabled and Not enabled. Tick the box on a row to show that map on the grid, use its On/Off button to enable or disable it, and click the Steam logo to open its Workshop page. Click any row to see it in Mod Details. Quick Select adds maps that don't share cells with your current selection.\n\nDEPENDENCIES\nMods required by enabled or selected map mods. Hover over one to see which maps need it. Always check a map's Workshop page for any additional requirements.\n\nCHECKS\nLists shared cells, vanilla area overlaps, missing dependencies and disabled dependencies for your enabled and selected map mods. Hover over a check to find out more.\n\nTHE GRID\nHover over a cell to see which maps occupy it. Zoom with the mouse wheel or the zoom buttons. When zoomed in, drag the grid or use the arrow keys (Shift: 5 cells) to move around. Press Fit or double-click the grid to see cells 0-60 and every selected or enabled map mod. To list only the map mods that use a cell, pick it with the X and Y dropdowns and press Filter Maps. Hide Vanilla removes the vanilla maps from the grid, so overlaps with them no longer show yellow, but Checks still lists them.\n\nPurple: map mod.\nLight purple: selected map mod that is not enabled.\nRed: map mods that share cells.\nYellow: map mod overlapping a vanilla town.\nGreen: vanilla town.\nBlue: Ohio River.\n\nShared cells can work with some maps and a careful load order, but check the Workshop pages of those maps first. Overlapping a vanilla town is usually intentional.\n\nPRESETS\nChoose a preset to apply it. Presets only change map mods and their dependencies, so your other mods stay as they are, and Undo reverts them. Save stores your enabled map mods, load orders and selected maps. Share copies the chosen preset to the clipboard, and Add imports one pasted from Share or an exported mapmodmanager.txt.\n\nLOAD ORDER\nAdjust the ModID and MapFolder load orders of active map mods and dependencies. You usually only need to if cells are shared.\n\nEXPORT\nWrites your selected subscribed maps, their dependencies and the multiplayer data for your server config to Zomboid/Lua/path/mapmodmanager.txt.\n\nChanges are only saved when you press Accept. Back discards them, and Undo/Redo step through them.",
